Dialogue: 0,0:00:37.17,0:00:39.11,Default,,0,0,0,,It's time to do
Dialogue: 0,0:01:05.51,0:01:07.47,Default,,0,0,0,,Do you guys see what I see?
Dialogue: 0,0:01:09.61,0:01:10.77,Default,,0,0,0,,That's Obelisk!
Dialogue: 0,0:01:10.99,0:01:12.93,Default,,0,0,0,,Kaiba must have brought him back!
Dialogue: 0,0:01:13.23,0:01:16.63,Default,,0,0,0,,Yeah, but Yugi's Egyptian\Ngod card is still gone!
Dialogue: 0,0:01:17.37,0:01:18.20,Default,,0,0,0,,What?
Dialogue: 0,0:01:18.28,0:01:21.31,Default,,0,0,0,,How's Yugi gonna stand up\Nto Obelisk without Slifer?
Dialogue: 0,0:01:22.67,0:01:23.67,Default,,0,0,0,,All right!
Dialogue: 0,0:01:24.51,0:01:25.45,Default,,0,0,0,,Tristan, no!
Dialogue: 0,0:01:25.71,0:01:26.87,Default,,0,0,0,,Get up, Joey!
Dialogue: 0,0:01:27.31,0:01:28.19,Default,,0,0,0,,Please, let's go!
Dialogue: 0,0:01:28.27,0:01:31.31,Default,,0,0,0,,Tristan, what are you\Ndoing? It's all good.
Dialogue: 0,0:01:32.15,0:01:34.81,Default,,0,0,0,,Trust me, Joey needs to see this.
Dialogue: 0,0:01:35.07,0:01:36.67,Default,,0,0,0,,It might make him wake up.
Dialogue: 0,0:01:37.59,0:01:38.51,Default,,0,0,0,,But how?
Dialogue: 0,0:01:38.77,0:01:41.13,Default,,0,0,0,,He'll see that Yugi's in trouble. So?
Dialogue: 0,0:01:41.31,0:01:44.13,Default,,0,0,0,,So, that should be enough\Nto snap him out of it.
Dialogue: 0,0:01:45.87,0:01:49.85,Default,,0,0,0,,Tristan, please, be careful\Nwith my brother. I will.
Dialogue: 0,0:01:50.15,0:01:52.73,Default,,0,0,0,,Now, come on, Joey, I\Nknow you can hear me.
Dialogue: 0,0:01:53.07,0:01:54.17,Default,,0,0,0,,Wake up, man.
Dialogue: 0,0:01:54.57,0:01:57.63,Default,,0,0,0,,Yugi's in trouble, and he\Nneeds your help now, Joey.
Dialogue: 0,0:02:01.73,0:02:05.55,Default,,0,0,0,,Your Egyptian God card won't\Nbe around for long, Kaiba.
Dialogue: 0,0:02:05.91,0:02:07.33,Default,,0,0,0,,That doesn't matter.
Dialogue: 0,0:02:07.71,0:02:10.00,Default,,0,0,0,,Obelisk has served his purpose already.
Dialogue: 0,0:02:10.09,0:02:13.31,Default,,0,0,0,,I won't be needing his\Nservices to finish you off.
Dialogue: 0,0:02:14.87,0:02:16.17,Default,,0,0,0,,Very well, then.
Dialogue: 0,0:02:16.41,0:02:20.33,Default,,0,0,0,,I'll place one card face\Ndown and end my turn.
Dialogue: 0,0:02:20.73,0:02:21.99,Default,,0,0,0,,Your move, Kaiba.
Dialogue: 0,0:02:22.37,0:02:24.49,Default,,0,0,0,,Well, as you've already pointed out,
Dialogue: 0,0:02:24.83,0:02:27.71,Default,,0,0,0,,it's time for Obelisk to\Nreturn to the graveyard.
Dialogue: 0,0:02:28.27,0:02:30.77,Default,,0,0,0,,Now, my Egyptian god card, be gone!
Dialogue: 0,0:02:37.81,0:02:43.19,Default,,0,0,0,,The wrath of Obelisk may be over,\Nbut the worst part is yet to come.
Dialogue: 0,0:02:43.43,0:02:45.97,Default,,0,0,0,,So I'd suggest you start\Nliving in the moment
Dialogue: 0,0:02:46.05,0:02:49.31,Default,,0,0,0,,and forget all that\Nnonsense about the past!
Dialogue: 0,0:02:54.39,0:02:57.13,Default,,0,0,0,,but then again there's\Nnothing you can do to
Dialogue: 0,0:02:57.21,0:02:59.93,Default,,0,0,0,,save yourself at this\Npoint as soon as i make
Dialogue: 0,0:03:00.01,0:03:03.57,Default,,0,0,0,,my next move your\Nhistory it can't end like
Dialogue: 0,0:03:03.65,0:03:06.65,Default,,0,0,0,,this i have to defeat\Nkaiba to get to merrick
Dialogue: 0,0:03:06.73,0:03:09.35,Default,,0,0,0,,it's the only way to stop his evil plan
Dialogue: 0,0:03:09.43,0:03:11.79,Default,,0,0,0,,because if the three\Negyptian god cards in my
Dialogue: 0,0:03:11.87,0:03:14.35,Default,,0,0,0,,millennium puzzle fall\Ninto merrick's hands the
Dialogue: 0,0:03:14.43,0:03:17.31,Default,,0,0,0,,world could meet the same\Nfate it did in the past
Dialogue: 0,0:03:18.79,0:03:19.77,Default,,0,0,0,,Come on!
Dialogue: 0,0:03:19.97,0:03:21.07,Default,,0,0,0,,Wake up, Joey!
Dialogue: 0,0:03:24.41,0:03:27.23,Default,,0,0,0,,Gotta keep fighting... the Yu-Gi!
Dialogue: 0,0:03:28.75,0:03:32.46,Default,,0,0,0,,Ladies and gentlemen, the tournament\Nfinals are about to begin!
Dialogue: 0,0:03:33.03,0:03:34.97,Default,,0,0,0,,Where did the gang disappear to?
Dialogue: 0,0:03:37.29,0:03:39.17,Default,,0,0,0,,They couldn't have gone too far.
Dialogue: 0,0:03:41.13,0:03:42.21,Default,,0,0,0,,What's up, guys?
Dialogue: 0,0:03:42.69,0:03:43.93,Default,,0,0,0,,What happened to you?
Dialogue: 0,0:03:44.13,0:03:46.77,Default,,0,0,0,,One second you were cheering me\Non, and the next you were gone!
Dialogue: 0,0:03:46.85,0:03:50.67,Default,,0,0,0,,We're not responsible for what\Nhappens to us in your dream, Joey.
Dialogue: 0,0:03:50.77,0:03:55.65,Default,,0,0,0,,So let's thank our lucky stars we're not\Nbeing chased by giant man-eating tomatoes.
Dialogue: 0,0:03:56.09,0:03:59.61,Default,,0,0,0,,Now, as I recall, you've got a\Nvery important duel to fight.
Dialogue: 0,0:03:59.69,0:04:01.11,Default,,0,0,0,,You made it to the finals.
Dialogue: 0,0:04:01.19,0:04:03.21,Default,,0,0,0,,Yeah, now we're getting somewhere.
Dialogue: 0,0:04:03.53,0:04:07.47,Default,,0,0,0,,I'm gonna duel my way straight to the\Ntop, and no one's gonna stand in my way.
Dialogue: 0,0:04:07.55,0:04:09.02,Default,,0,0,0,,You heard it here, folks.
Dialogue: 0,0:04:09.23,0:04:10.45,Default,,0,0,0,,I am the man.
Dialogue: 0,0:04:11.47,0:04:13.95,Default,,0,0,0,,Uh, Joey, the match is starting? Oh, yeah.
Dialogue: 0,0:04:14.03,0:04:16.97,Default,,0,0,0,,Now remember, everything\Nyou need is in your deck.
Dialogue: 0,0:04:17.11,0:04:19.19,Default,,0,0,0,,You just have to believe in your cards,
Dialogue: 0,0:04:19.27,0:04:21.91,Default,,0,0,0,,and a little bit of luck\Nwouldn't hurt either.
Dialogue: 0,0:04:21.99,0:04:24.81,Default,,0,0,0,,Who needs luck when you've\Ngot skills like mine?
Dialogue: 0,0:04:27.19,0:04:28.96,Default,,0,0,0,,Duelists, take your positions.
Dialogue: 0,0:04:29.73,0:04:31.73,Default,,0,0,0,,All right, I want a nice, clean duel.
Dialogue: 0,0:04:31.81,0:04:33.83,Default,,0,0,0,,You'll each start with 2,000 life points.
Dialogue: 0,0:04:33.91,0:04:36.63,Default,,0,0,0,,and direct attacks on your\Nopponent are not allowed.
Dialogue: 0,0:04:36.71,0:04:39.75,Default,,0,0,0,,Now shake hands, and when the\Nbell rings, come out dueling.
Dialogue: 0,0:04:39.83,0:04:41.01,Default,,0,0,0,,Good luck. You too.
Dialogue: 0,0:04:45.85,0:04:48.55,Default,,0,0,0,,This seems like more\Nthan just a dream. It's
Dialogue: 0,0:04:48.63,0:04:51.87,Default,,0,0,0,,like I gotta win this\Nfight at all costs Alright,
Dialogue: 0,0:04:52.21,0:04:56.15,Default,,0,0,0,,if the two opponents are ready,\Nthen we'll begin the duel right now
Dialogue: 0,0:04:57.35,0:04:58.59,Default,,0,0,0,,Start the duel
Dialogue: 0,0:04:59.17,0:05:01.91,Default,,0,0,0,,You're in trouble now, Wheeler. My move.
Dialogue: 0,0:05:03.01,0:05:06.21,Default,,0,0,0,,Now I play Neko Gal number one.
Dialogue: 0,0:05:09.65,0:05:10.93,Default,,0,0,0,,Not bad, huh?
Dialogue: 0,0:05:11.09,0:05:15.93,Default,,0,0,0,,Big deal. It's my move. Let's\Nsee, M-Warrior number one?
Dialogue: 0,0:05:16.15,0:05:18.50,Default,,0,0,0,,This guy's only got 1,000 attack points.
Dialogue: 0,0:05:18.97,0:05:19.95,Default,,0,0,0,,Remember, Joey,
Dialogue: 0,0:05:20.13,0:05:23.99,Default,,0,0,0,,a monster's strength is not always\Nthe key to winning in duel monsters.
Dialogue: 0,0:05:24.07,0:05:27.89,Default,,0,0,0,,Combining your monsters with magic\Ncards is often more important.
Dialogue: 0,0:05:28.89,0:05:30.15,Default,,0,0,0,,Grandpa has a point.
Dialogue: 0,0:05:31.15,0:05:33.33,Default,,0,0,0,,I play M-Warrior number one.
Dialogue: 0,0:05:37.43,0:05:39.01,Default,,0,0,0,,But that's not all.
Dialogue: 0,0:05:39.21,0:05:42.31,Default,,0,0,0,,I'll also throw in the\Nmagic card Legendary Sword.
Dialogue: 0,0:05:48.33,0:05:52.23,Default,,0,0,0,,That increases my warrior's\Nattack points by a whopping 300.
Dialogue: 0,0:05:52.83,0:05:54.89,Default,,0,0,0,,So read it and wink, Junior.
Dialogue: 0,0:05:56.07,0:05:57.73,Default,,0,0,0,,Now for the fun part.
Dialogue: 0,0:05:57.95,0:05:59.83,Default,,0,0,0,,And warrior, attack his monster.
Dialogue: 0,0:06:10.99,0:06:12.27,Default,,0,0,0,,Not bad, huh?
Dialogue: 0,0:06:12.35,0:06:13.85,Default,,0,0,0,,There's more to come.
Dialogue: 0,0:06:14.15,0:06:16.27,Default,,0,0,0,,Well, now it's my turn, so look out.
Dialogue: 0,0:06:16.43,0:06:17.49,Default,,0,0,0,,You're going down.
Dialogue: 0,0:06:17.63,0:06:18.49,Default,,0,0,0,,All right.
Dialogue: 0,0:06:18.85,0:06:21.11,Default,,0,0,0,,First, I'll place one card face down.
Dialogue: 0,0:06:21.97,0:06:25.29,Default,,0,0,0,,Then I'll play this bad\Nboy known as Lesser Dragon.
Dialogue: 0,0:06:27.71,0:06:29.01,Default,,0,0,0,,Take it away, Wheeler.
Dialogue: 0,0:06:29.19,0:06:30.53,Default,,0,0,0,,The pleasure's all mine.
Dialogue: 0,0:06:30.61,0:06:32.91,Default,,0,0,0,,I'm afraid you got a\Nlot to learn, Half-Pint.
Dialogue: 0,0:06:32.99,0:06:35.97,Default,,0,0,0,,You should have played your\Nlittle dragon in defense mode.
Dialogue: 0,0:06:36.05,0:06:37.52,Default,,0,0,0,,Ah, well, live and learn.
Dialogue: 0,0:06:37.97,0:06:39.45,Default,,0,0,0,,M-Warrior, do your stuff.
Dialogue: 0,0:06:39.53,0:06:43.19,Default,,0,0,0,,Blast his Lesser Dragon into\Nthe next millennium right now!
Dialogue: 0,0:06:44.49,0:06:46.21,Default,,0,0,0,,Not so fast, Wheeler!
Dialogue: 0,0:06:46.65,0:06:47.61,Default,,0,0,0,,Watch this!
Dialogue: 0,0:06:48.39,0:06:49.39,Default,,0,0,0,,A trap!
Dialogue: 0,0:06:49.81,0:06:52.69,Default,,0,0,0,,But not just any trap,\Nit's called reinforcement,
Dialogue: 0,0:06:53.41,0:06:56.53,Default,,0,0,0,,and it raises the attack\Npoints of my monster by 500!
Dialogue: 0,0:06:59.59,0:07:01.69,Default,,0,0,0,,Say goodbye to your warrior!
Dialogue: 0,0:07:05.07,0:07:07.05,Default,,0,0,0,,Yeah, burned to a crisp!
Dialogue: 0,0:07:07.55,0:07:08.39,Default,,0,0,0,,Not cool.
Dialogue: 0,0:07:09.59,0:07:11.89,Default,,0,0,0,,You call yourself a duelist, Wheeler?
Dialogue: 0,0:07:12.07,0:07:15.54,Default,,0,0,0,,If that's your best, I'm gonna\Ndestroy you one, two, three!
Dialogue: 0,0:07:16.37,0:07:17.51,Default,,0,0,0,,We'll see, kid.
Dialogue: 0,0:07:19.65,0:07:22.35,Default,,0,0,0,,I summon Tiger Action Attack Mode!
Dialogue: 0,0:07:25.05,0:07:26.87,Default,,0,0,0,,What do you say to that, twerp?
Dialogue: 0,0:07:27.39,0:07:28.95,Default,,0,0,0,,Is that all you got?
Dialogue: 0,0:07:33.09,0:07:35.57,Default,,0,0,0,,Go ahead and make your move, Diver.
Dialogue: 0,0:07:39.53,0:07:41.55,Default,,0,0,0,,This duel has grown tiresome.
Dialogue: 0,0:07:41.77,0:07:46.19,Default,,0,0,0,,The outcome is of no consequence to me\Nas long as a winner is declared soon.
Dialogue: 0,0:07:46.27,0:07:50.43,Default,,0,0,0,,For no matter who wins this,\NI will be the ultimate victor.
Dialogue: 0,0:07:53.13,0:07:57.27,Default,,0,0,0,,All right, now it's time to\Nbury the past and move on.
Dialogue: 0,0:07:57.61,0:08:02.17,Default,,0,0,0,,If you want to believe that we\Ndueled 5,000 years ago, be my guest.
Dialogue: 0,0:08:03.87,0:08:07.37,Default,,0,0,0,,But don't waste your time trying\Nto convince me that it's true.
Dialogue: 0,0:08:07.45,0:08:12.19,Default,,0,0,0,,I believe in only one thing, and\Nthat's my supreme dueling skills, Yugi!
Dialogue: 0,0:08:12.91,0:08:14.75,Default,,0,0,0,,Everything else is meaningless!
Dialogue: 0,0:08:15.45,0:08:16.45,Default,,0,0,0,,Now then,
Dialogue: 0,0:08:16.67,0:08:21.32,Default,,0,0,0,,let's get on with this duel so I can\Nfinally reclaim what I rightfully deserve!
Dialogue: 0,0:08:21.61,0:08:24.39,Default,,0,0,0,,The title that you stole from me, Yugi!
Dialogue: 0,0:08:24.77,0:08:27.87,Default,,0,0,0,,I will be known as the\Nworld's greatest duelist!
Dialogue: 0,0:08:29.23,0:08:31.53,Default,,0,0,0,,I'm afraid this is the final turn!
Dialogue: 0,0:08:33.13,0:08:34.07,Default,,0,0,0,,It's over!
Dialogue: 0,0:08:34.15,0:08:37.49,Default,,0,0,0,,I switch Lord of Dragon to defense mode
Dialogue: 0,0:08:40.25,0:08:44.69,Default,,0,0,0,,Then I activate the magic card\NThe Flute of Summoning Dragon.
Dialogue: 0,0:08:46.73,0:08:50.15,Default,,0,0,0,,This can mean only one thing\NI take it you're familiar
Dialogue: 0,0:08:50.23,0:08:54.27,Default,,0,0,0,,with my strategy As soon as\Nmy Lord of Dragons plays this
Dialogue: 0,0:08:54.35,0:08:58.13,Default,,0,0,0,,Flute. Two more dragons will be\Nsummoned to the field. You're
Dialogue: 0,0:08:58.21,0:09:01.21,Default,,0,0,0,,planning to call forth two\Nmore Blue-Eyes White Dragons,
Dialogue: 0,0:09:01.29,0:09:02.12,Default,,0,0,0,,aren't you?
Dialogue: 0,0:09:02.20,0:09:04.37,Default,,0,0,0,,That's precisely what I'm doing, Yugi!
Dialogue: 0,0:09:18.41,0:09:20.71,Default,,0,0,0,,How can I fight off three blue eyes?
Dialogue: 0,0:09:24.95,0:09:27.71,Default,,0,0,0,,Now I summon Steel Ogre Grotto!
Dialogue: 0,0:09:27.95,0:09:30.21,Default,,0,0,0,,And I'll place him in attack mode!
Dialogue: 0,0:09:31.85,0:09:34.59,Default,,0,0,0,,That tin can has 1,400 attack points.
Dialogue: 0,0:09:34.81,0:09:37.39,Default,,0,0,0,,That's enough to tear\Nmy tiger axe to shreds.
Dialogue: 0,0:09:37.47,0:09:39.61,Default,,0,0,0,,Come on, this is my dream.
Dialogue: 0,0:09:40.89,0:09:43.33,Default,,0,0,0,,I'm not really sure what you mean by that,
Dialogue: 0,0:09:43.41,0:09:46.29,Default,,0,0,0,,but you better wake up\Nand smell the duo-wheeler.
Dialogue: 0,0:09:46.79,0:09:48.97,Default,,0,0,0,,Because the worst is about to come.
Dialogue: 0,0:09:49.45,0:09:51.23,Default,,0,0,0,,It's called polymerization.
Dialogue: 0,0:09:51.45,0:09:54.09,Default,,0,0,0,,and I'm using it to\Nfuse my ogre grotto and
Dialogue: 0,0:09:54.17,0:09:58.03,Default,,0,0,0,,my lesser dragon together\Nto form Metal Dragon.
Dialogue: 0,0:09:59.47,0:10:02.49,Default,,0,0,0,,Now, my metal dragon, destroy his tiger!
Dialogue: 0,0:10:06.79,0:10:09.15,Default,,0,0,0,,Look, kid, this duel's not done.
Dialogue: 0,0:10:10.21,0:10:13.67,Default,,0,0,0,,By the way you're playing, I\Ndidn't know this duel even started.
Dialogue: 0,0:10:13.75,0:10:14.58,Default,,0,0,0,,Real funny.
Dialogue: 0,0:10:14.73,0:10:16.75,Default,,0,0,0,,I'm gonna make you eat those words.
Dialogue: 0,0:10:16.83,0:10:18.03,Default,,0,0,0,,So watch the master.
Dialogue: 0,0:10:19.13,0:10:20.25,Default,,0,0,0,,Flame Swordsman?
Dialogue: 0,0:10:20.95,0:10:23.69,Default,,0,0,0,,He only has 1,800 attack points.
Dialogue: 0,0:10:24.01,0:10:25.59,Default,,0,0,0,,Normally, that wouldn't be so bad.
Dialogue: 0,0:10:25.67,0:10:28.79,Default,,0,0,0,,But this kid's metal dragon has 1,850.
Dialogue: 0,0:10:29.39,0:10:32.98,Default,,0,0,0,,I'm going to have to play it\Nsafe and protect my life points.
Dialogue: 0,0:10:33.09,0:10:36.33,Default,,0,0,0,,Now I summon Hero of the\NEast in defense mode.
Dialogue: 0,0:10:36.87,0:10:38.53,Default,,0,0,0,,I hope that helps.
Dialogue: 0,0:10:40.61,0:10:42.53,Default,,0,0,0,,This is Rescue Copter 1.
Dialogue: 0,0:10:42.77,0:10:44.67,Default,,0,0,0,,We're approaching Chimacorp Island.
Dialogue: 0,0:10:44.75,0:10:45.58,Default,,0,0,0,,Over.
Dialogue: 0,0:10:54.39,0:10:58.75,Default,,0,0,0,,Looks like I have four monsters\Non the field now and you all.
Dialogue: 0,0:10:58.83,0:11:02.35,Default,,0,0,0,,you've got is your dark magician\Nand your pathetic magnet warrior
Dialogue: 0,0:11:02.43,0:11:08.27,Default,,0,0,0,,yuki and you know what that means\Ni can annihilate them and wipe
Dialogue: 0,0:11:08.35,0:11:12.99,Default,,0,0,0,,Out your life points, just give.
Dialogue: 0,0:11:13.07,0:11:16.47,Default,,0,0,0,,up now oh no i'm out of options
Dialogue: 0,0:11:20.37,0:11:22.59,Default,,0,0,0,,what do you think is\Ngoing on up there guys
Dialogue: 0,0:11:22.67,0:11:25.03,Default,,0,0,0,,let's hope that yuki's\Nwinning so this whole
Dialogue: 0,0:11:25.11,0:11:28.53,Default,,0,0,0,,nightmare can end already everything's
Dialogue: 0,0:11:28.61,0:11:32.39,Default,,0,0,0,,gonna be just fine guys\Nisn't that right joey
Dialogue: 0,0:11:35.41,0:11:38.45,Default,,0,0,0,,Okay, now I play the\Nmagic card, Stop Defense
Dialogue: 0,0:11:39.53,0:11:40.36,Default,,0,0,0,,What?
Dialogue: 0,0:11:40.65,0:11:41.94,Default,,0,0,0,,You heard what I said,
Dialogue: 0,0:11:42.03,0:11:45.41,Default,,0,0,0,,Wheeler I'm using my Stop\NDefense magic card to switch
Dialogue: 0,0:11:45.49,0:11:49.43,Default,,0,0,0,,your Hero of the East from\NDefense to Attack Mode Now,
Dialogue: 0,0:11:49.59,0:11:52.41,Default,,0,0,0,,Metal Dragon, attack\Nand destroy his monster
Dialogue: 0,0:11:56.59,0:12:01.09,Default,,0,0,0,,Aw, not again I can't believe this\Nkid is dueling circles around me
Dialogue: 0,0:12:02.51,0:12:07.07,Default,,0,0,0,,I place one card face down on the\Nfield. That's all for now. And remember,
Dialogue: 0,0:12:07.27,0:12:11.33,Default,,0,0,0,,you only have 300 life points So\Nnext turn, you're a goner Aw, yeah?
Dialogue: 0,0:12:11.61,0:12:13.79,Default,,0,0,0,,I got a plan. Don't you worry
Dialogue: 0,0:12:14.69,0:12:19.77,Default,,0,0,0,,Shield and sword I wish I really did have\Na plan But what am I supposed to do with a
Dialogue: 0,0:12:19.85,0:12:24.53,Default,,0,0,0,,magic card That switches the attack and\Ndefense points Of every monster on the field
Dialogue: 0,0:12:24.61,0:12:28.45,Default,,0,0,0,,Let's see. That metal dragon\Nof his has 1,700 defense.
Dialogue: 0,0:12:28.53,0:12:31.77,Default,,0,0,0,,points So if I use my shield\Nand sword with magic card,
Dialogue: 0,0:12:31.93,0:12:34.43,Default,,0,0,0,,his dragon's attack points become 1700.
Dialogue: 0,0:12:35.35,0:12:37.73,Default,,0,0,0,,That means all I gotta\Ndo is play a monster
Dialogue: 0,0:12:37.81,0:12:40.37,Default,,0,0,0,,with higher defense points\Nthan his metal dragon.
Dialogue: 0,0:12:40.45,0:12:43.11,Default,,0,0,0,,The problem is, I don't have one.
Dialogue: 0,0:12:43.33,0:12:45.53,Default,,0,0,0,,It doesn't really matter what you play.
Dialogue: 0,0:12:45.61,0:12:50.02,Default,,0,0,0,,Don't you know it's way too late for\Nyou to turn this duel around, Wheeler?
Dialogue: 0,0:12:50.59,0:12:52.49,Default,,0,0,0,,What would Yugi do right now?
Dialogue: 0,0:12:53.15,0:12:56.93,Default,,0,0,0,,Remember, always look closely\Nand consider all of your options.
Dialogue: 0,0:12:57.55,0:12:59.15,Default,,0,0,0,,Wait, that's it.
Dialogue: 0,0:12:59.23,0:13:03.77,Default,,0,0,0,,All I have to do is use that magic\Ncard on his metal dragon first.
Dialogue: 0,0:13:04.07,0:13:08.01,Default,,0,0,0,,And if all goes well, I should be\Nable to send it to the graveyard.
Dialogue: 0,0:13:08.37,0:13:09.21,Default,,0,0,0,,Here goes.
Dialogue: 0,0:13:09.59,0:13:13.41,Default,,0,0,0,,First, I'll summon a good buddy\Nof mine known as Flame Swordsman.
Dialogue: 0,0:13:15.25,0:13:19.93,Default,,0,0,0,,Wait, your metal dragon is a wind\Nattribute monster, isn't it? Yeah.
Dialogue: 0,0:13:20.65,0:13:22.05,Default,,0,0,0,,Then I can use this.
Dialogue: 0,0:13:22.45,0:13:25.37,Default,,0,0,0,,Now I activate my gust fan magic card.
Dialogue: 0,0:13:26.55,0:13:30.89,Default,,0,0,0,,It raises your monster's attack\Npoints, but lowers its defense points.
Dialogue: 0,0:13:31.79,0:13:32.95,Default,,0,0,0,,That was pointless.
Dialogue: 0,0:13:33.31,0:13:37.35,Default,,0,0,0,,Why would you waste your magic card\Njust to make my monster even stronger?
Dialogue: 0,0:13:37.43,0:13:38.93,Default,,0,0,0,,The pressure's getting to you.
Dialogue: 0,0:13:39.01,0:13:42.13,Default,,0,0,0,,Here I am about to end\Nthis duel in one more turn.
Dialogue: 0,0:13:42.33,0:13:46.05,Default,,0,0,0,,And instead of helping yourself, you\Nmake it even easier for me to win.
Dialogue: 0,0:13:46.13,0:13:47.84,Default,,0,0,0,,What kind of duelist are you?
Dialogue: 0,0:13:48.41,0:13:51.29,Default,,0,0,0,,They're kind of kick's\Nbutt, so check this out.
Dialogue: 0,0:13:51.57,0:13:53.73,Default,,0,0,0,,It's my shield and sword magic card.
Dialogue: 0,0:13:53.81,0:13:56.01,Default,,0,0,0,,Didn't see that one coming, did you?
Dialogue: 0,0:13:57.45,0:14:00.73,Default,,0,0,0,,Now you get why I lowered\Nyour monster's defense points?
Dialogue: 0,0:14:00.81,0:14:02.55,Default,,0,0,0,,Well, allow me to explain it.
Dialogue: 0,0:14:02.83,0:14:05.43,Default,,0,0,0,,My shield and sword magic\Ncard switches the attack
Dialogue: 0,0:14:05.51,0:14:08.21,Default,,0,0,0,,and defense points of\Nevery monster on the field.
Dialogue: 0,0:14:08.29,0:14:10.59,Default,,0,0,0,,That means your monster's stronger now.
Dialogue: 0,0:14:10.71,0:14:12.03,Default,,0,0,0,,Now you're catching on, shorty.
Dialogue: 0,0:14:12.11,0:14:14.63,Default,,0,0,0,,Flame Swordsman, attack as Metal Dragon!
Dialogue: 0,0:14:19.05,0:14:21.27,Default,,0,0,0,,Say goodbye to old Metal Mouth now.
Dialogue: 0,0:14:22.01,0:14:22.84,Default,,0,0,0,,What?
Dialogue: 0,0:14:23.81,0:14:25.73,Default,,0,0,0,,My swordsman just bit the dust.
Dialogue: 0,0:14:25.93,0:14:27.17,Default,,0,0,0,,What's going on here?
Dialogue: 0,0:14:27.33,0:14:30.07,Default,,0,0,0,,My Castle Walls Trap Card, that's what.
Dialogue: 0,0:14:30.29,0:14:32.39,Default,,0,0,0,,Looks like I'm one step ahead of you.
Dialogue: 0,0:14:32.47,0:14:35.03,Default,,0,0,0,,I sprung my card before you sprung yours.
Dialogue: 0,0:14:35.25,0:14:36.37,Default,,0,0,0,,Wait, you did what?
Dialogue: 0,0:14:36.49,0:14:39.11,Default,,0,0,0,,I added 500 defense points to my dragon,
Dialogue: 0,0:14:39.39,0:14:43.19,Default,,0,0,0,,which, thanks to your magic card,\Nincreased its attack points instead.
Dialogue: 0,0:14:43.27,0:14:44.23,Default,,0,0,0,,I get it.
Dialogue: 0,0:14:44.47,0:14:49.47,Default,,0,0,0,,Because of me, your metal dragon was able\Nto overpower my flame swordsman. Bingo.
Dialogue: 0,0:14:49.69,0:14:52.83,Default,,0,0,0,,And I have a feeling you know what\Nthis means, don't you, Wheeler?
Dialogue: 0,0:14:52.91,0:14:55.29,Default,,0,0,0,,Your monster's attack points were 1,600,
Dialogue: 0,0:14:55.37,0:14:59.03,Default,,0,0,0,,and my monster's attack\Npoints were raised to 2,000.
Dialogue: 0,0:15:00.13,0:15:02.81,Default,,0,0,0,,That means I lose 400 life points now.
Dialogue: 0,0:15:03.11,0:15:04.07,Default,,0,0,0,,I'm finished.
Dialogue: 0,0:15:05.49,0:15:07.99,Default,,0,0,0,,The duel is over. I won.
Dialogue: 0,0:15:08.57,0:15:09.77,Default,,0,0,0,,You beat me.
Dialogue: 0,0:15:10.31,0:15:11.27,Default,,0,0,0,,You know what?
Dialogue: 0,0:15:11.41,0:15:14.65,Default,,0,0,0,,I dueled my hardest today,\Nand that's all that matters.
Dialogue: 0,0:15:16.41,0:15:17.31,Default,,0,0,0,,Nice duel.
Dialogue: 0,0:15:17.55,0:15:19.43,Default,,0,0,0,,You had some great moves out there.
Dialogue: 0,0:15:19.51,0:15:20.34,Default,,0,0,0,,Thanks.
Dialogue: 0,0:15:20.42,0:15:21.91,Default,,0,0,0,,You weren't so bad yourself.
Dialogue: 0,0:15:22.91,0:15:25.91,Default,,0,0,0,,That shield and sword switch\Nyou pulled out there was great.
Dialogue: 0,0:15:25.99,0:15:26.82,Default,,0,0,0,,I'm serious.
Dialogue: 0,0:15:27.01,0:15:28.65,Default,,0,0,0,,One of the best I've ever seen.
Dialogue: 0,0:15:28.73,0:15:31.08,Default,,0,0,0,,Sorry I said some mean things about you.
Dialogue: 0,0:15:31.51,0:15:33.97,Default,,0,0,0,,It's all good, Shorty. Smell you later.
Dialogue: 0,0:15:34.65,0:15:37.67,Default,,0,0,0,,Thanks again for an awesome\Nduel, Wheeler. Sure.
Dialogue: 0,0:15:38.01,0:15:40.21,Default,,0,0,0,,And best of luck in the finals, all right?
Dialogue: 0,0:15:40.29,0:15:43.07,Default,,0,0,0,,I'll never forget that\Nsweet move you taught me.
Dialogue: 0,0:15:43.15,0:15:45.89,Default,,0,0,0,,Maybe I'll use it in\Nthe finals. Thank you.
Dialogue: 0,0:15:48.77,0:15:50.75,Default,,0,0,0,,This is where it all ends, Yugi.
Dialogue: 0,0:15:50.83,0:15:54.83,Default,,0,0,0,,There's no way you can escape the\Ndevastation of my three blue eyes.
Dialogue: 0,0:15:55.01,0:15:57.89,Default,,0,0,0,,The moment I've been\Nwaiting for is finally here!
Dialogue: 0,0:15:58.13,0:15:59.15,Default,,0,0,0,,Ha ha ha ha!
Dialogue: 0,0:15:59.33,0:16:00.45,Default,,0,0,0,,Ha ha ha ha!
Dialogue: 0,0:16:01.97,0:16:03.41,Default,,0,0,0,,I'm in major trouble!
Dialogue: 0,0:16:03.69,0:16:05.59,Default,,0,0,0,,With three blue eyes white dragons,
Dialogue: 0,0:16:05.67,0:16:09.79,Default,,0,0,0,,Kaiba can easily wipe out both of my\Nmonsters and the rest of my life points!
Dialogue: 0,0:16:09.87,0:16:10.99,Default,,0,0,0,,What am I gonna do?
Dialogue: 0,0:16:12.23,0:16:15.41,Default,,0,0,0,,It looks like the end of\Nthe line for the Pharaoh.
Dialogue: 0,0:16:15.85,0:16:20.45,Default,,0,0,0,,Which means Seto Kaiba will be the\Nnext casualty on the Shadow Realm.
Dialogue: 0,0:16:20.83,0:16:22.99,Default,,0,0,0,,Now my three blue eyes, attack!
Dialogue: 0,0:16:23.91,0:16:26.17,Default,,0,0,0,,Finish him off and end this duel!
Dialogue: 0,0:16:27.55,0:16:28.38,Default,,0,0,0,,No!
Dialogue: 0,0:16:31.99,0:16:35.53,Default,,0,0,0,,Once my dragons attack,\Nthis duel is over, Yugi!
Dialogue: 0,0:16:37.65,0:16:38.93,Default,,0,0,0,,Hold on, Yugi.
Dialogue: 0,0:16:39.45,0:16:40.28,Default,,0,0,0,,Shall we?
Dialogue: 0,0:16:40.45,0:16:42.31,Default,,0,0,0,,Yep, the one and only, pal.
Dialogue: 0,0:16:42.75,0:16:44.67,Default,,0,0,0,,I'm about to lose this duel!
Dialogue: 0,0:16:44.99,0:16:46.11,Default,,0,0,0,,Guess again, Yugi.
Dialogue: 0,0:16:46.39,0:16:47.71,Default,,0,0,0,,It's like you always tell me.
Dialogue: 0,0:16:47.79,0:16:50.23,Default,,0,0,0,,Look closely and consider\Nall of your options.
Dialogue: 0,0:16:50.31,0:16:51.53,Default,,0,0,0,,All of my options?
Dialogue: 0,0:16:52.41,0:16:53.24,Default,,0,0,0,,Yep.
Dialogue: 0,0:16:53.32,0:16:55.35,Default,,0,0,0,,I think you'll find a\Ncard that can save you.
Dialogue: 0,0:16:56.63,0:16:57.46,Default,,0,0,0,,Let's see.
Dialogue: 0,0:16:57.54,0:16:58.37,Default,,0,0,0,,He's right!
Dialogue: 0,0:16:58.55,0:16:59.67,Default,,0,0,0,,There's still hope!
Dialogue: 0,0:17:00.91,0:17:05.79,Default,,0,0,0,,Nice try, Yugi, but you're no\Nlonger the top-ranked duelist. What?
Dialogue: 0,0:17:06.69,0:17:08.61,Default,,0,0,0,,It's Red-Eyes Black Dragon!
Dialogue: 0,0:17:09.53,0:17:11.19,Default,,0,0,0,,Where did that come from?
Dialogue: 0,0:17:11.45,0:17:12.47,Default,,0,0,0,,If you recall,
Dialogue: 0,0:17:12.73,0:17:16.63,Default,,0,0,0,,you used your flute of summoning dragon\Nto summon your blue eyes to the field.
Dialogue: 0,0:17:16.71,0:17:20.87,Default,,0,0,0,,But you may have forgotten that\Nyour flute works on my hand as well.
Dialogue: 0,0:17:22.05,0:17:25.95,Default,,0,0,0,,So I owe you a thank you\Nfor bringing out this card,
Dialogue: 0,0:17:26.21,0:17:29.50,Default,,0,0,0,,which is a gift from a very\Nclose friend of mine, Kaiba.
Dialogue: 0,0:17:35.09,0:17:37.21,Default,,0,0,0,,This doesn't change a thing, Yugi.
Dialogue: 0,0:17:37.65,0:17:40.33,Default,,0,0,0,,I can destroy you and your red eyes.
Dialogue: 0,0:17:40.59,0:17:44.11,Default,,0,0,0,,Kaiba, don't be so sure of that, you fool.
Dialogue: 0,0:17:44.19,0:17:49.67,Default,,0,0,0,,Now, my blue-eyes white dragons will\Ndestroy all three of your monsters!
Dialogue: 0,0:17:51.05,0:17:52.35,Default,,0,0,0,,Attack now!
Dialogue: 0,0:17:53.03,0:17:55.31,Default,,0,0,0,,Annihilate his Dark Magician first!
Dialogue: 0,0:17:58.21,0:18:00.89,Default,,0,0,0,,Say goodbye to your favorite monster!
Dialogue: 0,0:18:01.55,0:18:02.99,Default,,0,0,0,,Not so fast, Kaiba!
Dialogue: 0,0:18:03.25,0:18:04.29,Default,,0,0,0,,Activate Trap!
Dialogue: 0,0:18:06.17,0:18:07.47,Default,,0,0,0,,Magician selection?
Dialogue: 0,0:18:07.89,0:18:10.25,Default,,0,0,0,,That protects your Dark\NMagician from my attack!
Dialogue: 0,0:18:10.33,0:18:13.77,Default,,0,0,0,,Which means you and your\Nmonster will escape unharmed!
Dialogue: 0,0:18:14.19,0:18:15.37,Default,,0,0,0,,That's right, Kaiba.
Dialogue: 0,0:18:15.47,0:18:19.55,Default,,0,0,0,,But my trap also sends your weakest\Nmonster to the card graveyard.
Dialogue: 0,0:18:22.77,0:18:25.77,Default,,0,0,0,,Fine, but you'll never\Nescape my other two attacks.
Dialogue: 0,0:18:28.97,0:18:33.13,Default,,0,0,0,,Beta, the Magnet Warrior is\Ngone, and your Red Eyes is next.
Dialogue: 0,0:18:33.43,0:18:35.35,Default,,0,0,0,,So much for Wheeler's gift.
Dialogue: 0,0:18:35.49,0:18:37.20,Default,,0,0,0,,That's what you think, Kaiba.
Dialogue: 0,0:18:37.65,0:18:39.31,Default,,0,0,0,,Reveal face-down card.
Dialogue: 0,0:18:42.07,0:18:45.09,Default,,0,0,0,,My Spellbinding Circle card\Nputs an end to your Blue
Dialogue: 0,0:18:45.17,0:18:50.57,Default,,0,0,0,,Eyes attack! And lowers its\Nstrength by 700. Nice try, Kaiba.
Dialogue: 0,0:18:51.85,0:18:54.27,Default,,0,0,0,,Time for Red Eyes to fight back
Dialogue: 0,0:18:55.29,0:19:00.31,Default,,0,0,0,,Destroy his Blue Eyes White\NDragon with Inferno Fire Blast
Dialogue: 0,0:19:07.77,0:19:12.49,Default,,0,0,0,,All right, you may have saved yourself\Nfor now, but this duel's far from done.
Dialogue: 0,0:19:14.87,0:19:19.49,Default,,0,0,0,,Well, it looks like I made it out of\Nthat mess, and I owe it all to you, Joey.
Dialogue: 0,0:19:19.93,0:19:23.22,Default,,0,0,0,,All I did was remind you of\Nthe advice that you gave me.
Dialogue: 0,0:19:23.49,0:19:25.63,Default,,0,0,0,,Now, win this fight, pal.
Dialogue: 0,0:19:25.93,0:19:26.89,Default,,0,0,0,,You too, Joey.
Dialogue: 0,0:19:30.71,0:19:31.87,Default,,0,0,0,,Hey, guys, look!
Dialogue: 0,0:19:32.75,0:19:33.99,Default,,0,0,0,,He's waking up!
Dialogue: 0,0:19:34.95,0:19:36.39,Default,,0,0,0,,Are you okay, Joey?
Dialogue: 0,0:19:42.39,0:19:45.85,Default,,0,0,0,,I must admit, Yugi's\Nmove took me by surprise.
Dialogue: 0,0:19:46.29,0:19:50.29,Default,,0,0,0,,But if he thinks this is the time\Nto celebrate, he's sadly mistaken.
Dialogue: 0,0:19:50.51,0:19:52.17,Default,,0,0,0,,Victory will be mine!
Dialogue: 0,0:19:52.53,0:19:54.03,Default,,0,0,0,,I have a long way to go,
Dialogue: 0,0:19:54.29,0:19:58.27,Default,,0,0,0,,but as long as I have faith in the\Nheart of the cards and in my friends,
Dialogue: 0,0:19:58.35,0:20:00.07,Default,,0,0,0,,I know I can win this!
Dialogue: 0,0:20:01.21,0:20:03.71,Default,,0,0,0,,Joey, say something!
